  "details": "# Issue:\n\nWhen looking at a world in the Main Menu, you can see the Instance Region and Population.\n\nDue to the fact that the US East / West Region need a character to declare them as East / West after the flag, the number for the Population needs to be moved around depending on if it's a US East / West or EU / JP instance.\n\nThis does not work correctly in the Main Menu however, there the Instance Population always has the distance to fit a character after the flag. The Quick Menu Here Tab & User Profile do not have that issue though, they adjust accordingly.\n\n# Expected Behavior:  \n\nThe Instance Population number should be moved closer / further away from the Instance Region flag in the Main Menu depending on if it's a US East / West or EU / JP instance. Just like it's done in the Quick Menu\n\n# Attachments:  \n\nHere are pictures showcasing the issue:",
